  "previewTake": "Miami's pass defense grades out at 3/100—genuinely among the worst in football—and we're bringing a pass offense graded at 77/100. That's the widest statistical edge on the board this week, and it's hard to overstate how badly that matchup tilts in our favor. The Dolphins' pass rush is equally anemic at 3/100, which should give our quarterbacks time to actually function. The real question is whether we can finish drives; we're +0.15 in net EPA over our last three games while Miami's been struggling at -0.06 over theirs. On the road at Hard Rock in an afternoon slot, this feels like a genuine opportunity—especially after dropping three of the last five head-to-heads against this division opponent."
